    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass with a clean build. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity across all four affected areas:\n\n**Identity derivation (V2, mixes in a fixed `V2` tag so every identifier changes):**\n- `Owner.getIdentityKey()` \u2014 added a shared `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` constant and prefixed the SHA-256 seed with `V2|`, so the key is cryptographically disjoint from v1.\n- `householdId(...)` in the controller \u2014 prefixed the seed with `V2|`, keeping it a pure function of last name + postcode (household grouping preserved).\n- `memberId(...)` \u2014 now uses a new `Localities.regionCodeV2(city, postcode)` (`\"V2\" + plainRegion`, e.g. `V2NSW`) as the `<REGION>` segment, so member ids like `V2NSW26786E13D55` never collide with any v1 value.\n\n**User-facing region stays plain (no `V2` leakage):**\n- `Localities.forOwner()` now derives the plain region directly from city/postcode instead of parsing it out of the (now `V2`-tagged) memberId prefix. So `locality` stays `NSW`, `timezone` and the owner-segment's `AREA` both derive from the plain region.\n\n**Response shape:**\n- Added an `OwnerIdentity` schema and grouped `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` under a nested `identity` object; removed them from the top level; added top-level integer `apiVersion: 2`. The `OwnerMapper` builds the nested object and sets `apiVersion`.\n\n**Audit schema + owner segment:**\n- The `OwnerCreatedEvent` moved to schema version 2: added `schemaVersion` (2) and `ownerSegment` recomputed from the v2 identity, while still carrying the owner id and the v2 memberId.\n\nRequest fields (`OwnerFields`) are unchanged. Full suite: **70 run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**",
