    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, traced from the code (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` and its call chain).\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Method-security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires the caller to hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (enforced unless security is disabled by the active config profile).\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` triggers JSR\u2011380 checks *before* any controller logic. Failures become `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 `400`. The constraints:\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max=10)`\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`, `@Email`\n\n## Inside the controller body (in this exact order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit (side-effect + read)** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` request header; if it was seen before, looks up the existing owner and returns it with `200 OK` (no new owner created). *(Not a validation, but it can end the flow early.)*\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** \u2014 via MapStruct `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`.\n5. **`applyAddress(owner)` (validation + mutation)** \u2014 resolves structured (`addressLine1/2`) vs. flat `address`, normalizes it (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`), and **throws `400`** if the address is blank after normalization.\n6. **Normalize telephone (mutation + validation)** \u2014 `normalizeTelephone(...)` converts to E.164; `validateNationalNumberLength(...)` **throws `400`** if the national number length is wrong for the country code (AU=9, US=10). The normalized value is set back on the owner.\n7. **Normalize email (mutation)** \u2014 `normalizeEmail(...)` lower-cases it.\n8. **`validateEmailDomain(email)` (validation)** \u2014 **throws `400`** if the domain is in the disposable-email blocklist.\n9. **`validatePostcode(postcode, city)` (validation)** \u2014 **throws `400`** if the postcode falls outside the city's allowed regional range.\n10. **Future registration-date check (validation)** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is after the server's current date, **throws `400`**.\n11. **Registration date normalization (mutation)** \u2014 defaults to today if null, then `toBusinessDay(...)` rolls weekends/public holidays forward; the result is set on the owner.\n12. **Daily-cap check (validation)** \u2014 counts existing owners registered on that business day; if `>= 100`, **throws `429`**.\n13. **Bulk-signup warning flag (mutation)** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when today's count `> 80`.\n14. **Household ID computation (mutation)** \u2014 normalizes last name, computes `householdId` (SHA\u2011256 of `V2|lastNameKey|postcode`), sets it, and gathers current household members.\n15. **Identity-uniqueness check (validation)** \u2014 if any non-deleted owner shares the same `identityKey` (telephone + email + last-name soundex), **throws `409`**.\n16. **Household-join determination** \u2014 computes whether this owner joins an existing household (based on `sharesHousehold` flag and email distinguishability).\n17. **City-capacity check (validation)** \u2014 counts owners in the same city; if `>= 50`, **throws `409`**.\n18. **Capacity-warning flag (mutation)** \u2014 sets `capacityWarning = true` when city count `>= 40`.\n19. **Derived-field population (mutations)** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount`, `householdSize`, and (if joining a household) a capped `membershipLevel`.\n20. **Soft duplicate detection (mutation)** \u2014 finds a possible duplicate (same postcode + last-name soundex, different identity); sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n21. **Member ID generation (mutation)** \u2014 builds a member ID (region + fiscal year + SHA\u2011256 hash + Luhn check digit) and de-duplicates it; sets `memberId`.\n\n## Persistence and post-save side-effects\n\n22. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`@Transactional`) \u2192 `ownerRepository.save(...)` (Spring Data JPA insert, `IDENTITY`-generated id). On flush, Hibernate enforces the **entity-level constraints**: `address`/`city`/`firstName`/`lastName` `@NotEmpty`, `telephone` `@Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")`, `email` `@Email`. *(No JPA lifecycle callbacks exist on `Owner`.)*\n23. **Record idempotency key (side-effect)** \u2014 stores `Idempotency-Key \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory map.\n24. **Audit log, human-readable (side-effect)** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: ...\")`.\n25. **Audit log, structured JSON event (side-effect)** \u2014 serializes an `OwnerCreatedEvent` (schemaVersion=2, incremented `OWNER_EVENT_SEQ`, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, ownerSegment) and logs it via `AUDIT`.\n26. **Notification log (side-effect)** \u2014 `NOTIFY.info(\"Welcome notification enqueued: ...\")`.\n27. **Response** \u2014 sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and returns the mapped `OwnerDto` with `201 CREATED`.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- Business-rule failures (steps 5\u201317) throw `ResponseStatusException` and are turned into HTTP responses by `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (`400`/`409`/`429`); DTO `@Valid` failures become `400` with per-field errors.\n- There is **no** custom owner validator, **no** `@InitBinder`, and **no** Spring `ApplicationEventPublisher` \u2014 the \"event\" is purely a log line. The only custom validator in the repo (`PetAgeValidator`) applies to pets, not owners.\n- The `CallMonitoringAspect` does **not** wrap this save, because `SpringDataOwnerRepository` isn't annotated `@Repository`.\n- The audit \"event,\" idempotency map, and event sequence counter are all **in-memory only** (not persisted, not published externally)."
